# Laravel Patterns

## Models
- One model per blueprint table; namespace by domain: `App\Models\Students\Student`
- Always define `$casts` for dates (datetime), decimals, JSONB
- Use `SoftDeletes` sparingly — prefer status fields for academic data
- Scope queries by academic year: `scopeForAcademicYear($query, $yearId)`

## Relationships
```php
// Enrollment belongs to student AND academic year
public function student(): BelongsTo
public function academicYear(): BelongsTo
public function section(): BelongsTo
```

## Services for Business Logic
Controllers stay thin. Complex logic in service classes:
- `EnrollmentService`, `AttendanceService`, `GradeEntryService`
- `CertificateGenerationService` (dispatches queue job)

## Queue Jobs for Heavy Operations
```php
// ❌ BAD — blocks HTTP request
foreach ($students as $student) { generateCertificate($student); }

// ✅ GOOD
GenerateCertificatesJob::dispatch($schoolId, $yearId)
    ->withIdempotencyKey("cert-{$schoolId}-{$yearId}");
```

## Audit
Log changes to academic records via `AuditService`:
```php
AuditService::log('updated', $enrollment, $oldValues, $newValues);
```

## Authorization
Use Laravel Policies scoped to school/role:
```php
$this->authorize('update', $enrollment);
```

## Eager Loading
```php
// ❌ N+1
Enrollment::all()->each(fn ($e) => $e->student->name);

// ✅
Enrollment::with(['student', 'section', 'academicYear'])->get();
```
